<title>BELGIUM: TABLE - BELGIAN MONEY MARKET SUPPLY CUT IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>TABLE - BELGIAN MONEY MARKET SUPPLY CUT IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said on Wednesday it withdrew liquidity from the money market in the week to August 11 to offset the widening efect of a fall in current acounts in francs and a decrease in bank notes in circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves		456.41 (+ 2.40)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security     13.53 (+ 0.35)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			     2.04 (- 0.06)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio			25.79 (unch)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	    106.89 (- 8.55)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation		464.52 (- 2.65)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
